
                         CNet/Codex BBS Menuset v1.02

                          (c) 1995 Sune Stjerneby

1.  Introduction
----------------

Some  weeks  ago,  i  downloaded  the file FPMENUS.LHA from Flux Point BBS.
This  archive  contained  the menuset of Flux Point BBS.  I found the menus
useful  and  effective,  but  i  never  could get used to the design.  So I
decided  to  re-write them totally.  I removed the ugly white double-border
and  replaced  it with a new, bevel-box (gadget) 3D-look.  I think they are
much more aestethically pleasing by now, and much more useful.

So,  if  you like these menus, feel free to use them.  But remember:  These
menus  are CallWare!  So if you use and like these menus, please call Codex
BBS  at  (+45)  56  27 67 30.  You will find tonnes of CNet and other Amiga
files here!


2.  Installation
----------------

Simply  copy all the files included to SYSTEXT:Menu/.  You may wish to back
up your old set first, in case you should not like my menus.

Then,  you  might  want to change some of the text, describing the commands
available  to the user.  This will primarily be neccessary on the mainmenu,
but it might also apply elsewhere.

